  "manual": [
    {
      "commodity": "GLOBAL",
      "why": "Fix is a DELETION of six dead relax_global entries, and the patch op-set has no delete/remove op. chocolate-milk 'chocolate\\s+milk', stuffing-mix 'stuffing', and the four '\\bspray\\b' relaxes (stain-remover, glass-cleaner, disinfectant-spray, air-freshener) string-equal NO token in GLOBAL_EXCLUDE (no 'spray', no 'stuffing' [only 'stuffed'], no 'chocolate'), so they waive nothing. Remove them by hand. KEEP stuffing-mix's other relaxes ('\\bmix\\b(?!...match)' and 'flavored').",
      "finding_summary": "Six relax_global entries are dead no-ops: they string-equal no GLOBAL_EXCLUDE token, so (since relax matching is exact-string) they waive nothing."
    },
    {
      "commodity": "grapes",
      "why": "Only suggested fix is relax_global ['\\bgum\\b'], which the verifier flagged as NOT regression-safe: relaxing '\\bgum\\b' would also admit grape bubble-gum and gumdrop candy into the grapes bucket. Zero board impact (blank size drops the 'Gum Drop' variety grape anyway) and the finding itself recommends leaving as-is. No safe op available.",
      "finding_summary": "A real 'Gum Drop' variety grape is knocked to unmatched by GLOBAL_EXCLUDE '\\bgum\\b', which grapes does not relax; fix is unsafe."
    },
    {
      "commodity": "shredded-cheese",
      "why": "fix_safe=false. Adding include 'cheese,?\\s+shredded' does NOT recover the item ('Hy-Vee natural cheese, shredded, chunk or sliced') because shredded-cheese's own exclude 'slice' still fires on 'sliced'. The only corrective is to narrow that 'slice' exclude, but any narrowing that stops matching 'sliced' (e.g. '\\bslices?\\b') would let genuine 'Sliced [variety] Cheese' products match shredded-cheese's '(cheddar|mozzarella|...)\\s+cheese' include and get stolen from the later sliced-cheese commodity. No regression-safe fix; low value (generic no-variety combo listing).",
      "finding_summary": "Item is genuinely UNMATCHED, but the suggested include is still blocked by the own 'slice' exclude firing on 'sliced'; narrowing 'slice' risks leaking real sliced cheese."
    }
  ]
